  "fuzz": "No new fuzz campaign: this change adds browser I/O orchestration over the existing bounded journal and backup validators. Actual worker tests exercise collection races, cancellation and storage failures. Previous validator fuzz reports retain their own scope.",
  "limitations": [
    "Only explicitly enumerated stores are covered; omitted stores or mutable external inventory cannot be inferred.",
    "This is a point-in-time journal snapshot, not a chain-state snapshot or freshness protection against malicious same-origin rollback.",
    "Writes after the common point require a later backup.",
    "Private backup encryption and durable export remain explicit caller actions.",
    "Allocation request IDs are not included in the existing recovery format; burned cursors and known addresses/exposures are retained.",
    "Coordinated live restore across all journal types remains separate work.",
    "No public-network transaction or real funds used."
